==Russian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{term|sc=Cyrs|врѣмѧ|tr=vrěmę|lang=cu}}. The so-called '''[[н]]'''-declension of this and nine other similar neuter nouns stems from the fact that the word-final '''-[[я]]''' was the nasal vowel [[Ѧ]], [[ѧ]] (little [[yus]]) in [[Old Church Slavonic]], resulting in the '''-ен-''' before all the case endings in the modern language. Compare Old East Slavic {{term|sc=Cyrs|веремя|tr=veremja|lang=orv}}, which is a regular East Slavic reflex of Late Proto-Slavic *{{term||sc=unicode|vermę}} by means of [[w:pleophony|pleophony]], as opposed to [[w:liquid metathesis|liquid metathesis]] which occured in Old Church Slavonic to resolve closed syllable.

